{
  "_comment": [
    "Made-up leaderboard data for developing against, in the exact shape",
    "/api/leaderboard returns. Toggled on from the leaderboard page itself, and",
    "only in a dev build -- every use of this file sits behind import.meta.env.DEV,",
    "so Vite drops both the toggle and this import from the production bundle.",
    "",
    "No names here: the board derives a handle from each playerId on the client",
    "(src/game/handle.ts), so these ids are what produce TranquilBison72.",
    "",
    "Words are real dictionary entries with their real Zipf frequencies, so the",
    "rarity badges and scores render exactly as they would with live data. Every",
    "find shares one date, moved to today at load, since the feed shows today only.",
    "",
    "Fifteen rows a board, because fifteen is what a board shows, and the",
    "player is seventh on both -- past the five rows on screen, which is where",
    "their own row sticks to the edge of the scrolling list rather than",
    "scrolling out of it. That is the case worth being able to look at: a",
    "player the board would otherwise hide for doing well.",
    "",
    "lastWeek / lastMonth are the champions of the two closed windows, shown on",
    "the plaque under each board -- different players from the ones leading now,",
    "since that is the interesting case.",
    "",
    "The feed is every word found on the day rather than one per player, so most",
    "of it is ordinary words with one or two finders. That is what it looks like",
    "live, and a fixture of nothing but Legends would not."
  ],
